  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry weather persists through the middle of the week. \nThunderstorms are possible Friday afternoon and evening, some of\nwhich may be strong with gusty winds and small hail.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nHigh pressure persists through the middle of the week with\nmostly dry weather and seasonable temperatures. Fog is possible\neach morning with any lingering low level moisture but will be\npatchy in nature and quickly dissipate around daybreak.\n\nA cold front crosses the area Friday on the leading edge of a \nfull latitude trough pushing into the region, with the added \nsupport of a northern stream shortwave pushing through the \ntrough around that time. With the potential for 500-1500 J/kg of\ninstability, 25-35KT of bulk shear and elongated, straight\nhodographs, there is a risk of some locally strong \nthunderstorms ahead of the front Friday afternoon, with the main\nthreat expected to be strong gusty winds. The greatest chance \nfor storms is likely to be concentrated over northern and \ncentral areas while more southern areas are likely to remain too\nstable due to southerly flow bringing in marine air. The inland\nextent of the marine layer will be key to watch for determining\nhow far south the severe threat extends.",
